$97E9 hud window tiles  | menu text				|
$97FF 					|						|
------------------------------------------------|

memory use table
$C000-$C01F test point list, each point is 2 bytes 1 for x and one for y. lines are processesed as point pairs, these must be stored such that x0 < x1
--$C009-$C019 line draw working mem-- this is getting moved to hram for speed reasons
$FF80-$FF86 line draw working memory
$C020 graphics buffer

alternate buffering method, could also use bg pallets to handle the buffering which would free up $8800-$97E8 on bank 1 this room could be used for more detailed tile sets for the window which gives more room for both the hud and menus, which could increase quality and allow for improvements like sub tile lettering to allow for more compact text and more text on screen.

for the line drawing ill use the background cordiates, as a test im going to make a table of lines at the begining of Wram and try and render them to the backgound, then ill try to animate it a bit by moving the points around.

for tile allocation for now im going to make a bit list where for some intiger number of tiles ill use a 0 to repesent an allocated tile and a 1 for unallocated tiles, then ill copy it into a regester then bit shift it left until the carry flag gets set while counting in another regester and the counted value (+ some offset) will be the first available tile, this could be a candidate for going into h-ram as it will be needed in both tile allocation and cleanup

Bresenhams algorothm implementiation, for the drawing of angled lines im going to try and implement bresenhams algorithm, from the wikipedia page for it (yeah im using wikipedia shoot me) i will be using the version described that uses 2 diffrent subroutenes and flips the inputs when needed. Im trying to figure out where to put the vareables of the psudo code from the wiki id prefer to only use regesters if possable i could keep hl pointing to the input points, but i always end up 1 regester short, so ill store all the relevent values in the pixel draw working mem area.
	memory use;
	b=x c=y $FF80=x0 $FF81=y0 $FF82=x1 $FF83=y1 $FF84=dx $FF85=dy $FF86=D
	
took me FAR too long to get my head around 2s compliment but as long as i just replace the D > 0 with a D < 128 i basicaly dont have to worry about the negitive numbers they just work, the only complication still to figure out, is the limit of 64 px horisontal displacement this places on drawn lines, this could be solved by using recoursive bisection. by halving the line and drawing it in two parts, this would use more memmory as you would need to store the midpoint, although it might be possable to use the stack to do this, it is also possable to handle this when queing the lines to be drawn as opposed to wnen actualy trying to draw the line. Im going to experement in another file to try and handle this using 16 aririthmatic as ive seen opcodes that can performe 16 bit arithmatic with the result landing in hl
	
